@title Motor at variable frequency at 1920: curves, readouts, model label, and the project without a motor
@area Simulate
@sizes 1920x1080
# The two-speed hoist fixture has a motor: Simulate > Motor at variable frequency shows the
# curves (each labelled with its frequency, rated and continuous lines labelled), the readout
# table, the model label and the folded list of what the model leaves out.
open qa/fixtures/hoist-two-speed.novo
wait 20
key ctrl+k
wait 3
text Motor at variable frequency
wait 4
key Enter
wait 30
expect "What this model leaves out"
expect "rated torque"
expect "Breakdown"
shot motor-curves
click_text "What this model leaves out"
wait 10
shot leaves-out-open
check_layout
# A project without a motor says so.
key Escape
wait 5
key ctrl+n
wait 20
key ctrl+k
wait 3
text Motor at variable frequency
wait 4
key Enter
wait 20
expect "no motor"
shot no-motor
